==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|dependent|-cy}} or {{af|en|dependence|-y}} or {{af|en|depend|-ency}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈpɛndənsi/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-dependency.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A state of dependence; a refusal to exercise initiative.
#: {{ux|en|Frank's sullen '''dependency''' was driving his father nuts.}}
# Something [[dependent]] on, or [[subordinate]] to, something else:
#: {{ux|en|In the United States' governmental structure, the military is conceived as a '''dependency''' under the executive branch.}}
# A [[colony]], or a [[territory]] [[subject]] to [[rule]] by an [[external]] [[power]].
#: {{syn|en|colony|protectorate|province|dominion}}
#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|page=201|passage=‘I have a little theory which you Messieurs who go out there must help me to prove. This is my share in the advantages my country shall reap from the possession of such a magnificent '''dependency'''.’}}
# A [[dependence]] on a [[habit]]-[[forming]] [[substance]] such as a [[drug]] or [[alcohol]].
#: {{syn|en|addiction}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} Reliance on the [[functionality]] provided by some other, [[external]] [[component]].
#: {{ux|en|This library has '''dependencies''' on a lot of other libraries. We have to compile all of those other libraries first.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} An external component whose functionality is relied on.
#: {{ux|en|One of this library's '''dependencies''' is very finicky. It can be hard to get it to compile on some systems.}}

